    "body": "Moving this explicitly to the [Stages](https://whatwg.org/stages) model. \n\nTo meet [Stage 1](https://whatwg.org/stages#stage1):\n\n- [X] A [comprehensive explainer](https://github.com/immersive-web/model-element/blob/main/explainer.md) for the [Contribution](https://whatwg.org/ipr-policy#21-contribution), in a standards organization-approved incubation venue such as a [W3C CG](https://www.w3.org/community/groups/) or a branch of an existing WHATWG Standard.\n- [ ] Consensus that the WHATWG is interested in exploring solutions in this problem space.\n- [X] (At least) one implementer interested in doing prototyping work: WebKit is prototyping, Meta and Samsung have expressed interest (potentially targeting Chromium).\n- [X] Identification of the [Contributor](https://whatwg.org/ipr-policy#contributor): @zachernuk (Apple). \n- [ ] Identification of a relevant WHATWG Workstream and Standard that will host the [Contribution](https://whatwg.org/ipr-policy#21-contribution), and notification of the Workstream Editor(s).\n\n@annevk, can you help us identify the right workstream? What's the appropriate mechanism for formally recording \"consensus that the WHATWG is interested in exploring solutions in this problem space\"?\n\n\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
